  // --- Progression tree. Keep identical in pvp.json and pvp-points.json. Each hero plays its home role from level 1:
  // the trunk is the hero above at levels 1..4, grown by the level formula from level 1 (health by
  // LevelHealthPercent, damage and healing by LevelDamagePercent per level), plus its "Line": "" entry's level-4
  // milestone (numbers at the hero's own scale). At 5 the tree forks: the home role goes on, or a second role opens
  // (Bolt's healer forks again at 8: healer or artillery); at 9 one branch splits into two kinds. A branch
  // ("Parent" = the branch it grows from, "" = the trunk; "From" = its first level) carries only the differences from
  // its parent with all the parent's milestones (a Super replaces the whole super). All numbers are at the hero's
  // level-1 scale and every node grows by the same formula, so a branch at 5 starts from the hero at 4 and a number it
  // leaves alone is one level up. Health and damage go on a branch only as role modifiers of the parent's:
  // "MaxHealthPercent" / "DamagePercent" (never lower than 85% health, 85% damage per charge, 70% for a healer —
  // TreeProgressionTests). The home role at 5 keeps everything the hero had at 4 and adds its role step. Profiles:
  // tank +30-40% HP, up to -15% damage, slower; assassin +25% damage, faster, -15% HP; healer heals teammates, -10..-20%
  // damage; sniper range and damage, slower charge; artillery farther and wider.
  // "Milestones" switch on from level "From" (4 on the trunk, 7 on a branch, 10 = the trick; a milestone "Super"
